<circuit version="1.1.0-SR2" rev="261119" stepSize="50000" stepsPS="20000000" NLsteps="100000" reaStep="50000" animate="0" >
<description>
# led_driver board on 230 V mains [SIMULATED]

The whole board as traced (`specs/SPEC.md` §3, test-13 values) around the MT7833A model (`../components/MT7833A`; its [INFERRED] numbers are listed in its README).

- **Input**: `MAINS` 230 V 50 Hz (325 V peak, floating) → `F1` (the board's T1A L 250 V glass fuse as a SimulIDE Fuse: T 1 A, 0.06 Ω, blows like the real one; right-click → Replace fuse) → bridge `D6`/`D8` (F1 side) and `D1`/`D5` → `C1` 100 nF, no bulk capacitor → `BUS` tunnel → IC1 DRAIN.
- **Start-up**: `R3` + `R6` (2 × 240 kΩ) from the bus into `C5` (VDD tunnel). Running, VDD comes from LED+ through `D2` / `R14A`.
- **Power stage**: `R10_11` = R10 ∥ R11 (0.65 Ω) on CS, freewheel `D3A`, `T1` 392 µH, `C7` 47 µF, bleeder `R16`. T1's `Cp` property, 17.9 pF, is its winding capacitance [from MEASURED, SPEC test 21, 2026-11-10; a separate capacitor `CW1` until 2026-11-14]; `D3A` has its measured C(V) (Cj0 14.67 pF, Vj 0.363 V, Mj 0.319, ≈ 4.1 pF over 0–62 V) [from MEASURED, SPEC test 22]; `CSW` 25.0 pF stands for the rest of the switch node's capacitance (MOSFET, copper), chosen so the total on pin 8 stays at the ≈ 47 pF used since 2026-11-05 [INFERRED, to be measured: the `csw` ring test]. T1's other end sits on C7, an AC ground, so the two add up. `C3` (22 pF on DSEN) is left out.
- **Loads** (close one switch): `SW_99` 99 Ω (the plan's known-good load, ≈ 31 V) and `SW_37` the lamp's own string as far as known: `LED37`, a **Led Strip** of 12 white LEDs at 2.78 V + 1 Ω each (33.36 V + 12 Ω, ≈ 37 V at 300 mA; label LED 12 W, CC 300 mA [PHOTO]; the per-LED knee and slope are [INFERRED], to fit to the measured V–I curve; Show State off, it would flag OVER on the ripple peaks above 300 mA). The 33 Ω load and the near-OVP string (`SW_33`, `SW_LED`) were removed on 2026-11-06; `board_mains_reference.sim1` still has them.
- **Scope**: CH1 VDD, CH2 CS, both relative to the IC ground (pin 8).

**Try it:** close `SW_99` and press play. VDD climbs to 18 V in ≈ 0.3 s, COMP pre-charges for ≈ 60 ms, then the output takes VDD over (24 V clamp) and `I_LED` settles at ≈ 0.31 A average with a 100 Hz ripple. `sim/board_scenarios.py` runs every load and reports the blink rate. About 0.04 s of wall time per simulated millisecond while switching (≈ 2.5 % of real time); `board_mains_reference.sim1` is the same board with a plain switch instead of the chip, for speed comparisons.
</description>


